Z||000000||DaveL||10-17-2000||02:51 PM||||Been really enjoying driving my 87 SE 2.5 Auto Ferraro(what my friends call it), btu I keep getting intermittent check engine soon light. It goes off pretty quickly after coming on,and the engine seems to run no different. A check of the codes reveals code 13 set twice, and code 24 set twice, both while driving.<BR>Could some one go into a little depth about possible causes of the codes, especially the 24??? I've had my cat replaced with a slight glasspack, but otherwise not modified the exhaust. Only did that because the old one got plugged.<BR>There should also have been a code for obnoxious passengers too!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Spyro86SE||10-17-2000||05:45 PM||||hey your dreaded code 13 is the oxygen sensor<BR>check for a sticking or misadjusted tps check wiring and connectors from oxygen sensor and 24 is vehicle speed sensor a fault in this circuit should be indicated when the car is moving disregard code 24 if it is set when the rear wheels are not turning check connections at the ecm and tps ||||reg||11
Z||000002||terryk||10-17-2000||10:49 PM||||Yeah, when they replaced the cat, they didn't reconnect the O2 or the VSS.<P>OOOOOOOOOrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr,<P>The O2 is DOA and the VSS is disconnected.<P>Or the wires are burnt through.<P>Check the connectors first.||||reg||1
